                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "28fadaba-42f3-3fb9-8578-489b85b5794d",
                        "entry_id": "7ebf6bf6-f329-3eac-aebb-450aaf4994ee",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. прийти в чувство"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b37eb3c3-f2c9-352e-b99a-c9d119850993",
                        "entry_id": "7ebf6bf6-f329-3eac-aebb-450aaf4994ee",
                        "glosses": [
                            "опомниться после какого-либо переживания, испуга"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c4828b5f-7cec-4665-82a0-8018ba34f785",
                                "sense_id": "b37eb3c3-f2c9-352e-b99a-c9d119850993",
                                "text": "Мужественная, все беды пережившая русская женщина первая опамятовалась. — Ах ты, туды твою мать! — сказала она. — Ну где тонко, там и рвётся! — Она ползала вокруг меня на коленях, скрепляла рану на шинели откуда-то из-под телогрейки добываемыми булавками и то материла себя, то стонала, один раз даже по башке своей долбанула, и ещё бы долбанула, да я руку её придержал."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ccb18e1a-8723-4a96-9d6c-8d12fd6b6511",
                        "source_entry_id": "7ebf6bf6-f329-3eac-aebb-450aaf4994ee",
                        "target_lang_word": "recollect",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "recollect",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "599e0a9b-feed-33bb-8ee5-e47ffb6e5059",
                                        "entry_id": "f642a103-1256-3298-8df7-503c6e71b233",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To recall; to collect one's thoughts again, especially about past events."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b3592d9-7d72-46c8-be9c-3d5b42506868",
                                                "sense_id": "599e0a9b-feed-33bb-8ee5-e47ffb6e5059",
                                                "text": "I remember the concert clearly, but I can't recollect why I had decided to go there."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f17d891-ab34-4700-bf11-41d4c0a9705b",
                                                "sense_id": "599e0a9b-feed-33bb-8ee5-e47ffb6e5059",
                                                "text": "I recollect taking a very poor view of the apparently inadequate cabs of the Stirling engines, as compared with those of the Brighton; there were even to be seen at this time a number of the completely cabless Cudworths."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "recollect",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5f21f8a3-26bc-3348-8671-98597d99e4ca",
                                        "entry_id": "d1a0e03d-cfea-3029-981b-8d80c81c3525",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To collect (things) together again."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7e1ea80-9800-3e40-a8a2-c6b056c4cafa",
                                        "entry_id": "d1a0e03d-cfea-3029-981b-8d80c81c3525",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To compose oneself."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c155fdb2-239b-407f-b202-5ced99043647",
                                                "sense_id": "e7e1ea80-9800-3e40-a8a2-c6b056c4cafa",
                                                "text": "The Tyrian queen […] Admir'd his fortunes, more admir'd the man; then re-collected stood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "803183c4-628b-40f5-a466-0b2aa725acb6",
                                                "sense_id": "e7e1ea80-9800-3e40-a8a2-c6b056c4cafa",
                                                "text": "The Major suddenly recollected himself, and withdrew his hand, and at the same time, threw himself into a chair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80d72074-c21b-40c1-85b5-b284802deb86",
                        "source_entry_id": "7ebf6bf6-f329-3eac-aebb-450aaf4994ee",
                        "target_lang_word": "recollect oneself",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6eaad992-465e-422c-8352-cd791e8bbddb",
                        "source_entry_id": "7ebf6bf6-f329-3eac-aebb-450aaf4994ee",
                        "target_lang_word": "remember oneself",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9f1da21d-b91c-4724-9284-faee8c5e419e",
                        "source_entry_id": "7ebf6bf6-f329-3eac-aebb-450aaf4994ee",
                        "target_lang_word": "come to oneself",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "come to oneself",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3868e3ab-35a9-3795-ace5-6fa4925a8f9c",
                                        "entry_id": "1e5bb03b-f089-3c2e-9b8f-6daba9eb3c08",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To gain consciousness or self-control."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87ee29f4-dcb6-48e2-a88e-b5bec021cd36",
                                                "sense_id": "3868e3ab-35a9-3795-ace5-6fa4925a8f9c",
                                                "text": "When I came to myself I was lying, not in the outer blackness of the Mohune vault, not on a floor of sand; but in a bed of sweet clean linen, and in a little whitewashed room, through the window of which the spring sunlight streamed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fa788b6-659f-412e-9fd8-dfecd20bda83",
                                                "sense_id": "3868e3ab-35a9-3795-ace5-6fa4925a8f9c",
                                                "text": "The patient invariably falls down in a swoon and is carried like dead to his hammock, where he is tightly lashed with cords. As they come to themselves, they writhe in agony, so that their hammocks rock violently to and fro."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7de627b4-ade2-4e97-8572-3fac81723dc8",
                        "source_entry_id": "7ebf6bf6-f329-3eac-aebb-450aaf4994ee",
                        "target_lang_word": "come to life",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "come to life",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7d5f3f3-269f-3150-88dc-1c8eaa639fb6",
                                        "entry_id": "8549d15e-310c-3408-ab27-50ed5ac67096",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To become alive, to be given life; to be brought into existence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41cb76ee-2bab-4cd4-aa5a-8c539b4a3619",
                                                "sense_id": "d7d5f3f3-269f-3150-88dc-1c8eaa639fb6",
                                                "text": "We want to know exactly how the first cells came to life on earth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c736854b-eb4b-4a42-8514-f2935985d8e2",
                                                "sense_id": "d7d5f3f3-269f-3150-88dc-1c8eaa639fb6",
                                                "text": "I don't think of Hobbes as a doll that miraculously comes to life when Calvin's around. Neither do I think of Hobbes as the product of Calvin's imagination... Hobbes is more about the subjective nature of reality than about dolls coming to life."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57ae51eb-78c5-3b0b-bf78-0b496ef78201",
                                        "entry_id": "8549d15e-310c-3408-ab27-50ed5ac67096",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To appear as if alive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65027bde-61ab-4c64-b859-7c6398e9c416",
                                                "sense_id": "57ae51eb-78c5-3b0b-bf78-0b496ef78201",
                                                "text": "The CGI-generated characters came to life through an incredible display of a cutting-edge 3D technology."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "06577208-0780-3c92-a332-2a150b60441d",
                                        "entry_id": "8549d15e-310c-3408-ab27-50ed5ac67096",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To start to become energetic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f646db3-1795-4ef0-86ea-7808edfe36c4",
                                                "sense_id": "06577208-0780-3c92-a332-2a150b60441d",
                                                "text": "It was only after Yakubu sliced another chance into the side netting, a bad miss by the former Everton striker, that Norwich came to life."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7fa10ac5-a5a1-45aa-8f9d-479420ec4f1c",
                        "source_entry_id": "7ebf6bf6-f329-3eac-aebb-450aaf4994ee",
                        "target_lang_word": "come round",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "come round",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93ab12b0-688c-3db0-ab6f-922904993fb0",
                                        "entry_id": "702f309e-66e0-3136-a4a9-f63ae1ba111e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To change direction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7f316c3-12d5-31a8-a5a6-7023945ee1a4",
                                        "entry_id": "702f309e-66e0-3136-a4a9-f63ae1ba111e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To change one's opinion to a prevailing one."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddcf3ffa-a7f8-4d4d-b8d9-1eab6734a5f3",
                                                "sense_id": "a7f316c3-12d5-31a8-a5a6-7023945ee1a4",
                                                "text": "I'll explain it again, and maybe he'll come round to my way of thinking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1d2be12-b66d-42a4-b509-7cea10f8ed24",
                                                "sense_id": "a7f316c3-12d5-31a8-a5a6-7023945ee1a4",
                                                "text": "He's a reasonable man. I knew he'd come round eventually."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc046a4c-1ed6-304b-b51b-0afaa7932cad",
                                        "entry_id": "702f309e-66e0-3136-a4a9-f63ae1ba111e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To return to a former condition.",
                                            "To recover consciousness, to come to"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb5c725f-c6da-4197-9cbd-9913451732f0",
                                                "sense_id": "bc046a4c-1ed6-304b-b51b-0afaa7932cad",
                                                "text": "After the blow to my head, I took a while to come round."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf85c71e-3e7f-480b-8145-6f14fd2148e3",
                                                "sense_id": "bc046a4c-1ed6-304b-b51b-0afaa7932cad",
                                                "text": "Signalman Bridges was killed by the blast, as was fireman Nightall. Amazingly, driver Gimbert came round some 200 yards away, on the grass outside the Station Hotel where he had been flung."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f690674d-38b0-326a-a95f-bc0d7b602e71",
                                        "entry_id": "702f309e-66e0-3136-a4a9-f63ae1ba111e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To return to a former condition.",
                                            "To cease anger or hostility."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96adc487-49ed-32a9-85d1-b67ea3c01f05",
                                        "entry_id": "702f309e-66e0-3136-a4a9-f63ae1ba111e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To visit someone's home or other regular place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd6a9a24-3507-459b-906f-a25762aa0acf",
                                                "sense_id": "96adc487-49ed-32a9-85d1-b67ea3c01f05",
                                                "text": "Would you like to come round for dinner tonight?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6acc2916-4820-437f-b566-302878d35952",
                                                "sense_id": "96adc487-49ed-32a9-85d1-b67ea3c01f05",
                                                "text": "What day does the garbage man come round?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16bf03a5-2983-4c93-a109-b71e15fbb869",
                                                "sense_id": "96adc487-49ed-32a9-85d1-b67ea3c01f05",
                                                "text": "That the young Mr. Churchills liked—but they did not like him coming round of an evening and drinking weak whisky-and-water while he held forth on railway debentures and corporation loans. Mr. Barrett, however, by fawning and flattery, seemed to be able to make not only Mrs. Churchill but everyone else do what he desired."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
